      "worked": "The domain is $\\mathbb R$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\left|\\lvert -x+1\\rvert-\\lvert -x-1\\rvert\\right|\\\\f(-x)&=\\left|\\lvert x-1\\rvert-\\lvert x+1\\rvert\\right|\\\\f(-x)&=\\left|-\\left(\\lvert x+1\\rvert-\\lvert x-1\\rvert\\right)\\right|\\\\f(-x)&=\\left|\\lvert x+1\\rvert-\\lvert x-1\\rvert\\right|\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
